* xbench.cal: the kernels of the benchmark.  tools/py/bench.py makes a
* program of them, for the CPU simulation and as a job for COS, runs it and
* reads the times; docs/DEVELOPMENT.md has how.
*
* This file is not a program by itself.  The lines that begin with a star
* and a letter divide it:
*
*   *I             what is done once, before anything is timed
*   *K name units group text
*                  a kernel.  What follows sets it up.  The time is the
*                  clock periods from *T to *E, read off the real-time
*                  clock, for as many repetitions as the word XREP holds;
*                  bench.py divides it by the repetitions and by the units,
*                  the elements one repetition works through.  What follows *E
*                  leaves a sum in S1 that depends on everything the
*                  kernel computed, and may be left out when *E finds it
*                  there.
*   *X             code behind the kernels
*   *D             data
*
* The rules a kernel keeps:
*
* - Its syntax is what both assemblers take, this repository's and the CAL
*   on the drive: every number above 7 with its base (D' or O'), no
*   comment behind an instruction, no macro, no symbol that reads like a
*   register (XA and VL1 do).
* - It sets every register it reads, and a repetition starts from what the
*   one before started from, so that the sum is the same for any number of
*   repetitions and the reference model can say what it has to be.
* - It reads the arrays ARRA, ARRB, IDXI and IDXJ and never writes them.
*   ARRC and WORK are anybody's.
* - The code from *T to *E is shorter than an instruction buffer (32 words),
*   and bench.py puts it at the start of one: its jumps stay in the buffer
*   unless leaving it is what the kernel is about.
* - What it leaves under way at *E it waits for: memory is waited for by
*   the program, a vector register by reading an element of it.
* - A7 counts the repetitions.  B00 belongs to the return jumps; B77 and
*   the names that begin with X belong to the program around the kernels,
*   which also uses A7, S6 and S7 at *E, before the sum is formed.
*
*I
         A1        0
         A2        N
         A5        D'1237
         A6        7
         S7        N-1
XBI1     A3        A1+1
         S1        +FA3
         S1        +FS1
         ARRA,A1   S1
         A4        A3+A3
         A4        A4+1
         S1        +FA4
         S1        +FS1
         ARRB,A1   S1
         A4        A1+A5
         S1        A4
         S1        S1&S7
         IDXI,A1   S1
         A4        A1*A5
         A4        A4+A6
         S1        A4
         S1        S1&S7
         IDXJ,A1   S1
         S1        0
         ARRC,A1   S1
         WORK,A1   S1
         A1        A1+1
         A0        A2-A1
         JAN       XBI1
*
* ARRA(i) = i + 1 and ARRB(i) = 2 i + 3 as floating-point numbers,
* IDXI(i) = (i + 1237) mod N, which leads through all N words and back to
* the first, and IDXJ(i) = (1237 i + 7) mod N, each number once, scattered.
*
*K EMPTY 4096 scalar a loop with nothing in it but its count
*T
         A7        XREP,0
EMP1     A1        0
         A2        N
EMP2     S1        S1
         A1        A1+1
         A0        A2-A1
         JAN       EMP2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       EMP1
*E
         S1        A1
*K SINT 4096 scalar integer work in registers: shifts, logic, bit counts, a product, sums
*T
         A7        XREP,0
INT1     S1        XSEED,0
         S3        0
         A6        0
         A1        N
INT2     S2        S1
         S2        S2<D'13
         S1        S1\S2
         S2        S1
         S2        S2>D'7
         S1        S1\S2
         S2        S1
         S2        S2<D'17
         S1        S1\S2
         A3        PS1
         A4        ZS1
         A5        A3*A4
         A6        A6+A5
         S3        S3+S1
         A1        A1-1
         A0        A1
         JAN       INT2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       INT1
*E
         S2        A6
         S1        S3\S2
*K SFP 4096 scalar floating point in registers: reciprocal, its correction, products, sums
*T
         A7        XREP,0
FLT1     S5        0
         A1        N
FLT2     S1        +FA1
         S1        +FS1
         S2        /HS1
         S3        S1*IS2
         S2        S2*FS3
         S4        S1*FS1
         S4        S4+FS2
         S5        S5+FS4
         A1        A1-1
         A0        A1
         JAN       FLT2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       FLT1
*E
         S1        S5
*K BRANCH 4096 scalar jumps inside a buffer: a pair is one that is not taken and one that is
*T
         A7        XREP,0
BRA1     A1        D'1024
         A2        1
         A3        0
BRA2     A0        A2
         JAZ       BRA9
         J         BRA3
BRA3     A3        A3+1
         JAM       BRA9
         J         BRA4
BRA4     A3        A3+1
         JAZ       BRA9
         J         BRA5
BRA5     A3        A3+1
         JAM       BRA9
         J         BRA6
BRA6     A3        A3+1
         A1        A1-1
         A0        A1
         JAN       BRA2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       BRA1
BRA9     S1        A3
*E
         S1        A3
*K CALL3 4096 fetch calls of three routines a buffer each: caller and routines stay in the four buffers
*T
         A7        XREP,0
CLN1     A1        D'512
         A6        0
CLN2     R         XF1
         R         XF2
         R         XF3
         R         XF1
         R         XF2
         R         XF3
         R         XF1
         R         XF2
         A1        A1-1
         A0        A1
         JAN       CLN2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       CLN1
*E
         S1        A6
*K CALL8 4096 fetch calls of eight routines a buffer each: nine blocks of code for four buffers
*T
         A7        XREP,0
CLF1     A1        D'512
         A6        0
CLF2     R         XF1
         R         XF2
         R         XF3
         R         XF4
         R         XF5
         R         XF6
         R         XF7
         R         XF8
         A1        A1-1
         A0        A1
         JAN       CLF2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       CLF1
*E
         S1        A6
*K SLOAD 4096 smem a scalar load in a loop
*T
         A7        XREP,0
SLD1     A1        0
         A2        N
SLD2     S1        ARRA,A1
         A1        A1+1
         A0        A2-A1
         JAN       SLD2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       SLD1
*E
*K SSTORE 4096 smem a scalar store in a loop
         S1        XSEED,0
*T
         A7        XREP,0
SSR1     A1        0
         A2        N
SSR2     ARRC,A1   S1
         A1        A1+1
         A0        A2-A1
         JAN       SSR2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       SSR1
*E
         A1        ARRC
         A2        N
         R         XCK
*K SCOPY 4096 smem two scalar loads, an add and a store
*T
         A7        XREP,0
SCP1     A1        0
         A2        N
SCP2     S1        ARRA,A1
         S2        ARRB,A1
         S3        S1+S2
         ARRC,A1   S3
         A1        A1+1
         A0        A2-A1
         JAN       SCP2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       SCP1
*E
         A1        ARRC
         A2        N
         R         XCK
*K CHASE 4096 smem a chain of loads, each from the address the one before brought
*T
         A7        XREP,0
CHS1     A1        N
         A3        0
         A4        0
CHS2     A3        IDXI,A3
         A4        A4+A3
         A1        A1-1
         A0        A1
         JAN       CHS2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       CHS1
*E
         S1        A4
*K RECUR 4096 smem a floating-point recurrence: load, subtract, multiply, store
*T
         A7        XREP,0
REC1     A1        0
         A2        N
         S3        0
         S4        0.4
REC2     S1        ARRB,A1
         S1        S1-FS3
         S3        S1*FS4
         ARRC,A1   S3
         A1        A1+1
         A0        A2-A1
         JAN       REC2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       REC1
*E
         A1        ARRC
         A2        N
         R         XCK
*K SIEVE 4096 smem the sieve of Eratosthenes: stores, loads and jumps on what was loaded
*T
         A7        XREP,0
SIV1     A1        0
         A2        N
         S1        1
SIV2     WORK,A1   S1
         A1        A1+1
         A0        A2-A1
         JAN       SIV2
         A3        2
         A5        D'64
         S2        0
SIV3     S0        WORK,A3
         JSZ       SIV6
         A4        A3*A3
SIV4     A0        A4-A2
         JAP       SIV6
         WORK,A4   S2
         A4        A4+A3
         J         SIV4
SIV6     A3        A3+1
         A0        A3-A5
         JAN       SIV3
         A1        2
         A6        0
SIV7     A5        WORK,A1
         A6        A6+A5
         A1        A1+1
         A0        A2-A1
         JAN       SIV7
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       SIV1
*E
         S1        A6
*K SORT 256 smem a Shell sort of 256 numbers: loads, compares and stores as the numbers fall
         A5        D'64
         VL        A5
*T
         A7        XREP,0
SRT1     A1        0
         A5        D'64
         A6        D'256
SRT0     A2        IDXJ
         A0        A2+A1
         V0        ,A0,1
         A2        WORK
         A0        A2+A1
         ,A0,1     V0
         A1        A1+A5
         A0        A6-A1
         JAN       SRT0
         A1        0
SRT2     A2        XGAP,A1
         A0        A2
         JAZ       SRT8
         A3        A2
SRT3     S1        WORK,A3
         A4        A3
SRT4     A5        A4-A2
         A0        A5
         JAM       SRT6
         S2        WORK,A5
         S0        S1-S2
         JSP       SRT6
         WORK,A4   S2
         A4        A5
         J         SRT4
SRT6     WORK,A4   S1
         A3        A3+1
         A0        A6-A3
         JAN       SRT3
         A1        A1+1
         J         SRT2
SRT8     A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       SRT1
*E
         A1        WORK
         A2        D'256
         R         XCK
*K VADD 32768 vreg a vector add of registers, 64 elements
         A5        D'64
         VL        A5
         A0        ARRA
         V0        ,A0,1
         A0        ARRB
         V1        ,A0,1
*T
         A7        XREP,0
VAD1     A4        D'512
VAD2     V2        V0+V1
         A4        A4-1
         A0        A4
         JAN       VAD2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       VAD1
         S1        V2,A0
*E
         R         XRED
*K VFP 16384 vreg floating-point vectors in registers: multiply, add, reciprocal, multiply, chained
         A5        D'64
         VL        A5
         A0        ARRA
         V0        ,A0,1
         A0        ARRB
         V1        ,A0,1
*T
         A7        XREP,0
VFL1     A4        D'256
VFL2     V2        V0*FV1
         V3        V2+FV0
         V4        /HV1
         V5        V3*FV4
         A4        A4-1
         A0        A4
         JAN       VFL2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       VFL1
         S1        V5,A0
*E
         V2        V5!V5
         R         XRED
*K VMIX 16384 vreg vectors in registers: logic, a mask and a merge, bit count, shift, integer add
         A5        D'64
         VL        A5
         A0        IDXI
         V0        ,A0,1
         A0        IDXJ
         V1        ,A0,1
*T
         A7        XREP,0
         A3        3
         S1        4
VMX1     A4        D'256
VMX2     V2        V0&V1
         V3        S1&V1
         VM        V3,N
         V4        V2!V0&VM
         V5        PV4
         V6        V4>A3
         V7        V5+V6
         A4        A4-1
         A0        A4
         JAN       VMX2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       VMX1
         S1        V7,A0
*E
         V2        V7!V7
         R         XRED
*K VLOAD 32768 vmem vector loads of 64 words in a row
         A5        D'64
         VL        A5
*T
         A7        XREP,0
         A6        D'8
         A7        A7*A6
VLD1     A1        ARRA
         A4        D'64
VLD2     A0        A1
         V0        ,A0,1
         A1        A1+A5
         A4        A4-1
         A0        A4
         JAN       VLD2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       VLD1
         S1        V0,A0
*E
         V2        V0!V0
         R         XRED
*K VSTORE 32768 vmem vector stores of 64 words in a row
         A5        D'64
         VL        A5
         A0        ARRA
         V0        ,A0,1
*T
         A7        XREP,0
         A6        D'8
         A7        A7*A6
VSR1     A1        ARRC
         A4        D'64
VSR2     A0        A1
         ,A0,1     V0
         A1        A1+A5
         A4        A4-1
         A0        A4
         JAN       VSR2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       VSR1
*E
         A1        ARRC
         A2        N
         R         XCK
*K VCOPY 16384 vmem two vector loads, an integer add and a vector store
         A5        D'64
         VL        A5
*T
         A7        XREP,0
         A6        4
         A7        A7*A6
VCP1     A1        ARRA
         A2        ARRB
         A3        ARRC
         A4        D'64
VCP2     A0        A1
         V0        ,A0,1
         A0        A2
         V1        ,A0,1
         V2        V0+V1
         A0        A3
         ,A0,1     V2
         A1        A1+A5
         A2        A2+A5
         A3        A3+A5
         A4        A4-1
         A0        A4
         JAN       VCP2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       VCP1
*E
         A1        ARRC
         A2        N
         R         XCK
*K VSTRIDE 4096 vmem vector loads of every sixteenth word
         A5        D'64
         VL        A5
*T
         A7        XREP,0
         A6        D'16
         A7        A7*A6
VSD1     A1        ARRA
         A3        D'1024
         A4        4
VSD2     A0        A1
         V0        ,A0,A6
         A1        A1+A3
         A4        A4-1
         A0        A4
         JAN       VSD2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       VSD1
         S1        V0,A0
*E
         V2        V0!V0
         R         XRED
*K GATHER 16384 vmem gathers: a load of 64 indices, then the 64 words they name
         A5        D'64
         VL        A5
         A0        ARRA
         V0        ,A0,1
*T
         A7        XREP,0
         A6        4
         A7        A7*A6
GAT1     A1        ARRA
         A2        IDXJ
         A4        D'64
         V3        V0\V0
GAT2     A0        A2
         V1        ,A0,1
         A0        A1
         V2        ,A0,V1
         V3        V3+V2
         A2        A2+A5
         A4        A4-1
         A0        A4
         JAN       GAT2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       GAT1
         S1        V3,A0
*E
         V2        V3!V3
         R         XRED
*K SCATTER 16384 vmem scatters: loads of 64 indices and 64 words, then the words to where the indices say
         A5        D'64
         VL        A5
*T
         A7        XREP,0
         A6        4
         A7        A7*A6
SCT1     A1        ARRC
         A2        IDXJ
         A3        ARRA
         A4        D'64
SCT2     A0        A2
         V1        ,A0,1
         A0        A3
         V0        ,A0,1
         A0        A1
         ,A0,V1    V0
         A2        A2+A5
         A3        A3+A5
         A4        A4-1
         A0        A4
         JAN       SCT2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       SCT1
*E
         A1        ARRC
         A2        N
         R         XCK
*K BLOCK 16384 vmem block transfers: 64 T registers from memory and back to it elsewhere
*T
         A7        XREP,0
         A6        4
         A7        A7*A6
         A5        D'64
BLK1     A1        ARRA
         A2        ARRC
         A4        D'64
BLK2     A0        A1
         T00,A5    ,A0
         A0        A2
         ,A0       T00,A5
         A1        A1+A5
         A2        A2+A5
         A4        A4-1
         A0        A4
         JAN       BLK2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       BLK1
*E
         A1        ARRC
         A2        N
         R         XCK
*K SAXPY 16384 vfp c = 3 a + b in floating point: two loads, multiply, add and store, chained
         A5        D'64
         VL        A5
*T
         A7        XREP,0
         A6        4
         A7        A7*A6
         A3        3
         S1        +FA3
         S1        +FS1
SAX1     A1        ARRA
         A2        ARRB
         A3        ARRC
         A4        D'64
SAX2     A0        A1
         V0        ,A0,1
         A0        A2
         V1        ,A0,1
         V2        S1*FV0
         V3        V2+FV1
         A0        A3
         ,A0,1     V3
         A1        A1+A5
         A2        A2+A5
         A3        A3+A5
         A4        A4-1
         A0        A4
         JAN       SAX2
         A7        A7-1
         A0        A7
         JAN       SAX1
*E
         A1        ARRC
         A2        N
         R         XCK
*K DOT 16384 vfp a dot product: two loads, a multiply and a running sum, and the 64 sums added up
         A5        D'64
         VL        A5
         A0        ARRA
         V0        ,A0,1
*T
         A7        XREP,0
         A6        4
         A7        A7*A6
DOT1     A1        ARRA
         A2        ARRB
         A4        D'64
         V4        V0\V0
DOT2     A0        A1
         V0        ,A0,1
         A0        A2
         V1        ,A0,1
         V2        V0*FV1
         V4        V4+FV2
         A1        A1+A5
         A2        A2+A5
         A4        A4-1
         A0        A4
